            "depth": 16.5,
            "radius": 8.25,
            "diameter": 16.5,
            "thickness": 1.7
          },
          "shapeClassification": "Torus + raised cathedral head + 4 prongs + round brilliant",
          "styleClassification": "Two-Tone Cathedral Solitaire",
          "settingType": "Four-Prong Cathedral",
          "parentComponent": null,
          "childComponents": [
            "Band Shank",
            "Cathedral Shoulders",
            "Prong Head",
            "Center Diamond"
          ],
          "confidenceScore": 0.91,
          "proceduralCADParameters": {
            "targetSoftware": "OpenSCAD",
            "primitives": [
              "rotate_extrude for half-round band (polygon profile)",
              "polygon + hull() for cathedral shoulder sweep",
              "linear_extrude for basket ring (annulus)",
              "hull() between two spheres for tapered prong claws",
              "cylinder(r1,r2,h) cone for brilliant-cut crown",
              "hull() between thin cylinders for pavilion cone"
            ],
            "booleanOperations": [
              "difference() for basket inner cut",
              "union() for assembly of all components"
            ],
            "transformations": [
              "rotate_extrude around Z-axis for band",
              "rotate() around Z at 0/90/180/270 for prongs",
              "translate() to absolute assemblyStack Z positions",
              "scaled geometry: stone table = girdle x 0.56; pavilion = girdle x 0.43"
            ],
            "customParameters": {
              "ring_inner_diameter": 16.5,
              "ring_outer_diameter": 19.9,
              "band_thickness_radial": 1.7,
              "band_thickness_z": 1.7,
              "shoulder_rise_height": 3.5,
              "shoulder_width_at_base": 1.7,
              "shoulder_angular_extent_base_deg": 56,
              "shoulder_angular_extent_top_deg": 36,
              "prong_count": 4,
              "prong_thickness": 0.6,
              "prong_extension_above_stone": 1.0,
              "prong_splay_radial_offset_mm": 0.3,
              "stone_diameter": 6.5,
              "stone_table_pct": 0.56,
              "stone_crown_height": 1.0,
              "stone_pavilion_pct": 0.43,
              "metal_shank": "yellow gold (#FFD700)",
              "metal_head_prongs": "white gold / platinum (#E5E4E2)",
              "gem_color_hex": "#E8F4FF",
              "cadConstructionGuide": {
                "bandApproach": "Build the band using rotate_extrude(angle=360) on a 2D polygon profile placed in the X-Y half-plane. The polygon has a flat inner edge at X = ring_inner_radius (8.25 mm), a vertical inner edge from band_bottom_z (-1.7) to band_top_z (0), short flat top and bottom segments leading into rounded outer corners (radius = edge_fillet_radius = 0.4 mm), and a straight outer edge at X = inner_radius + band_thickness_shoulder = 9.95 mm. The cross-section is half-round with rounded outer corners, fitting the crossSectionalShape type from the analysis. The minor radial taper (band_width_bottom 2.2 -> band_width_near_setting 2.8) is approximated by uniform radial thickness of 1.7 mm for visual simplicity; this is within measurement tolerance.",
                "settingApproach": "The cathedral head is built as two swept shoulder wedges plus a small basket ring. Each shoulder module is a hull() of quadrilateral cross-section polygons stacked from gallery_base_z (0 mm) to gallery_top_z (3.5 mm). The wedge sweeps from the band inner/outer radius (8.25/9.95 mm) at the base to the basket inner/outer radius (3.3/3.6 mm) at the top. The angular extent tapers from 28-degree half-angle at the base (56-degree total) to 18-degree half-angle at the top (36-degree total). Two shoulders are placed at angles 0 and 180. The basket is a linear_extrude(height=0.4) of a difference between two circles (outer 3.6, inner 3.3), positioned at Z = gallery_top_z - 0.4 to gallery_top_z = 3.1 to 3.5 mm. The basket provides a seat for the stone girdle at exactly stone_girdle_z = 3.5 mm.",
                "prongApproach": "Four prongs are placed at angular positions [0, 90, 180, 270] using a for() loop. Each prong module is a hull() between two spheres: a base sphere of radius 0.3 mm at (prong_base_radial_offset * cos(angle), prong_base_radial_offset * sin(angle), stone_girdle_z) and a tip sphere of radius 0.15 mm at (prong_tip_radial_offset * cos(angle), prong_tip_radial_offset * sin(angle), prong_tip_z). prong_base_radial_offset = 3.5 mm (just outside the stone girdle radius of 3.25 mm); prong_tip_radial_offset = 3.8 mm (splay offset = 0.3 mm outward, equivalent to ~10-degree splay angle over 2 mm height). Prong extends from prong_base_z = 3.5 mm to prong_tip_z = 5.5 mm, which is exactly 1.0 mm above stone_table_z = 4.5 mm, satisfying prong_extension_above_stone.",
                "stoneApproach": "Center stone is a round brilliant diamond. Crown is rendered as a cylinder(r1, r2, h) cone: r1 = gem_girdle_diameter/2 = 3.25 mm at stone_girdle_z = 3.5 mm; r2 = gem_table_diameter/2 = 1.82 mm at stone_table_z = 4.5 mm; h = 1.0 mm (crown height). Pavilion is rendered as hull() between a thin cylinder (radius 3.25 mm, height 0.01 mm) at stone_girdle_z and a point at pavilion_tip_z = stone_girdle_z - gem_pavilion_depth = 0.705 mm. Table percentage = 56% of girdle diameter; pavilion depth percentage = 43% of girdle diameter (2.795 mm). The stone is given alpha=0.7 on the crown and alpha=0.5 on the pavilion to suggest transparency of the diamond.",
                "assemblyOrder": [
                  "Build ring_band: rotate_extrude of half-round polygon profile, color ring_color",
                  "Build cathedral shoulders: for angles in [0, 180], hull() of swept wedge polygons, color ring_color",
                  "Build basket ring: linear_extrude of annular difference() at gallery_top_z - 0.4, color ring_color",
                  "Place 4 prongs: for(a = prong_angular_positions) rotate([0,0,a]) implicitly via positional math, color prong_color",
                  "Build center_stone crown: cylinder cone from girdle to table, color stone_color alpha 0.7",
                  "Build center_stone pavilion: hull() cone from girdle to pavilion tip, color stone_color alpha 0.5",
                  "Union() all components for final assembly"
                ],
                "criticalConstraints": [
                  "Stone girdle MUST sit at exactly stone_girdle_z = 3.5 mm (matches gallery_top_z and prong_base_z)",
                  "Prong tips must NOT exceed prong_tip_z = 5.5 mm; tip extends exactly 1.0 mm above stone_table_z = 4.5 mm, satisfying prong_extension_above_stone",
                  "Gallery inner radius at top (3.3 mm) MUST be >= stone girdle radius (3.25 mm) so cathedral shoulders do not clip into the stone crown",
                  "Gallery outer radius at top (3.6 mm) MUST be > stone girdle radius (3.25 mm) to fully encircle the girdle",
                  "Band inner radius MUST equal ring_inner_radius (8.25 mm) to provide correct finger clearance",
                  "All components must geometrically connect: shoulders bridge from band top (Z=0) to basket (Z=3.1-3.5); prongs emerge from basket; stone sits on basket with girdle resting at Z=3.5",
                  "Prong base radial offset (3.5 mm) MUST be > stone girdle radius (3.25 mm) so prongs do not clip into the table at radius 1.82 mm",
                  "Pavilion tip at Z=0.705 mm must lie inside the gallery volume (Z 0 to 3.5); alpha=0.5 makes it visually subtle inside the basket"
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
